('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',19,'Cordon, on the Portes du Mont-Blanc domain but not linked on skis','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.coverage.2.items.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','heading',2,'Which pass for which trip','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenariosTitle'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',20,'A week in Megève or Saint-Gervais','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.0.who'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',21,'The Évasion Mont-Blanc pass, at {{f:F000535}} for six days, or {{f:F000536}} online at least ten days ahead.',array['F000535','F000536']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.0.what'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',22,'A week in Combloux or La Giettaz','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.1.who'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',23,'The Portes du Mont-Blanc pass covers the smaller network for {{f:F000545}}.',array['F000545']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.1.what'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',24,'Families','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.2.who'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',25,'Children under 5 ski free, a child''s six days cost {{f:F000538}}, and four or more passes of the same length bought together, for at least two adults and two under 18, take a tenth off.',array['F000538']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.2.what'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',26,'First days on skis','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.3.who'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',27,'A beginner pass for the gentle lifts of Rochebrune and Mont d''Arbois costs {{f:F000543}} a day.',array['F000543']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.3.what'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',28,'Adding Chamonix','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.4.who'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',29,'Mont-Blanc Unlimited adds Chamonix and Courmayeur for {{f:F000546}} a day or {{f:F000547}} for six days.',array['F000546','F000547']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.4.what'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',30,'The whole winter','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.5.who'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','line',31,'A season pass costs {{f:F000541}}, or {{f:F000542}} bought before 30 November.',array['F000541','F000542']::text[],'review','loader','pass.scenarios.5.what'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','pass','note',1,'Children are 5 to 14, adults 15 to 64 and seniors 65 to 79; skiers over 80 pay half the adult rate at the ticket office.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','pass.after'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','heading',0,'Getting there and choosing a base','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.h2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','para',0,'By the fastest road Geneva airport is {{f:F000630}} from La Giettaz and {{f:F000631}} from Saint-Nicolas, Lyon airport {{f:F000632|n}} to {{f:F000633}} and Chambéry {{f:F000634|n}} to {{f:F000635}}. The motorway runs up the Arve valley to Sallanches and Le Fayet, and the villages lie a short climb above it.',array['F000630','F000631','F000632','F000633','F000634','F000635']::text[],'review','loader','access.paras.0'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','para',1,'Two railway stations serve the area. Sallanches-Combloux-Megève, {{f:F000636|n}} to {{f:F000637}} from the villages, has TGV trains from Paris and the Y83 bus on to Combloux, Demi-Quartier and Megève. At Saint-Gervais-le-Fayet the Valléen gondola has climbed from outside the station to Saint-Gervais since December 2024, with Altibus buses to the other resorts. In Megève the free Meg-Bus runs between the centre, Rochebrune, Le Jaillet, Mont d''Arbois and Côte 2000.',array['F000636','F000637']::text[],'review','loader','access.paras.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','para',2,'Megève, Saint-Gervais and Combloux fall under the Loi Montagne, which from November to March requires winter tyres on all four wheels or snow chains in the car. There are free car parks at the foot of the Princesse gondola and at Le Bettex, which makes the Megève network easy to start from by car.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.paras.2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','note',0,'Road distances are the fastest route by the OSRM router on OpenStreetMap data, without traffic or snow. Trains and buses: <a href="https://www.megeve-tourisme.fr/en/informations-pratiques/acces-et-mobilite/en-train/">Megève tourist office</a> (April 2026), <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/saint-gervais/transfer-guide">Snowcarbon</a> and <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=8172">Guide Ski for Megève</a>. Winter equipment rules: <a href="https://www.allopneus.com/guide-pratique/auto/conseils-pneu/loi-montagne-haute-savoie">Allopneus</a> (October 2026). Parking: <a href="https://www.ultimatefrance.com/?p=8770">Ultimate France</a> and <a href="https://tourism.saintgervais.com/i-want-to/an-activity/evasion-mont-blanc-ski-resort-saint-gervais-les-bains-en-4359378/">the Saint-Gervais tourist office</a>. 2026/27 bus timetables have not yet been checked.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.accessNote'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','heading',1,'How far each base reaches','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.basesH3'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','para',3,'Mont d''Arbois is the natural base. From Megève centre the Chamois gondola lifts straight into the network, and Rochebrune is {{f:F000599|w}} lift ride away. Princesse and Saint-Gervais sit on the far side of Mont d''Arbois: from Le Bettex a lift top above 2,000 m is {{f:F000610|w}} lift rides away.',array['F000599','F000610']::text[],'review','loader','access.basesParas.0'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','para',4,'Saint-Nicolas and Rochebrune lie at the ends. From Saint-Nicolas, Rochebrune takes {{f:F000611|w}} lift rides, and from Rochebrune, Saint-Nicolas takes {{f:F000597|w}}. Les Portes du Mont-Blanc is small enough that every base reaches the others in a few rides, but none of its lifts climbs above 2,000 m.',array['F000597','F000611']::text[],'review','loader','access.basesParas.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','caption',0,'Lift rides from each base in the Megève network','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.basesCaption'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',0,'To Rochebrune','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.baseCols.0'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',1,'To Saint-Gervais','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.baseCols.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',2,'To Saint-Nicolas','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.baseCols.2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',3,'To a lift top above 2,000 m','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.baseCols.3'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',4,'Megève, Rochebrune','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.0.base'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',5,'Megève centre, by the Chamois gondola','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.1.base'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',6,'Princesse','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.2.base'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',7,'Saint-Gervais','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.3.base'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','line',8,'Saint-Nicolas','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.bases.4.base'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','access','note',1,'Fewest lift rides from the village lifts before reaching the first lift of each area, on the OpenStreetMap model. Le Jaillet, Combloux and La Giettaz are left out because no lift or piste links them to these areas. Times are not included.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','access.basesNote'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','kicker',0,'Snowboarders','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.kicker'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','heading',0,'Riding Évasion Mont Blanc on a board','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.h2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','para',0,'The freestyle sits on Mont Joux, in the middle of the Megève network. Snowcarbon describes the Snowpark Mont Joux at the foot of the Mont Joux chair, with a hip, a big air, tables and rails, as the easiest park to reach from Saint-Gervais, and the Saint-Gervais tourist office lists a boardercross on the same mountain that emails each run as a video. Megève''s own park, Waidzai, lies above the village, and Combloux and La Giettaz keep smaller sets of features.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.paras.0'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','para',1,'The trees are the strength here. Snowcarbon sends riders into the Mont d''Arbois woods after fresh snow and into the Magic Garden between the Lanchettes and Radaz lifts above Rochebrune, and points intermediates to the powder under the chair above the Altiport. Ultimate France adds the Route Émile Allais, an ungroomed line down to Cassioz, between Praz-sur-Arly and Megève.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.paras.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','para',2,'The bigger lines need a guide. The back of Mont Joly, reached by the Mont Joly chair, and the north east slopes off Mont d''Arbois and Mont Joux are exposed to avalanches. Haute-Savoie tourism points to a well known freeride sector on Les Portes du Mont-Blanc, and Snowcarbon calls the steeper slopes of La Giettaz a full day out with few other people on them. On piste, Snowcarbon picks the run from L''Épaule down to Saint-Nicolas, and Ultimate France recommends the Épaule traverse above the village.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.paras.2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','para',3,'Drags are common. In the map data {{f:F000552}} of the {{f:F000551}} main lifts are drags; they make up {{f:F000564}} of the main lifts on Mont d''Arbois and {{f:F000594}} at La Giettaz, against none on Le Jaillet. All of the terrain beyond the markers is uncontrolled, so the avalanche bulletin and a local guide come first.',array['F000551','F000552','F000564','F000594']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.paras.3'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','heading',1,'Parks and places to ride','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.listTitle'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','snowboard','note',0,'Parks and off piste: <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/saint-gervais/ski-area">Snowcarbon for Saint-Gervais</a> and <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/megeve/ski-area">for Megève</a>, <a href="https://www.ultimatefrance.com/?p=8770">Ultimate France</a> (October 2026) and <a href="https://tourism.saintgervais.com/i-want-to/an-activity/evasion-mont-blanc-ski-resort-saint-gervais-les-bains-en-4359378/">the Saint-Gervais tourist office</a>. Drag lift shares from OpenStreetMap. Park layouts change every season, and off piste routes need a guide and the day''s avalanche bulletin.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.0.note'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','kicker',0,'Families','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.kicker'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','heading',0,'Holidays with children','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.h2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','para',0,'The pass is kind to the young: children under 5 ski free, and a family buying four or more passes of the same length together, with at least two adults and two under 18, takes a tenth off the total. Combloux holds the Famille Plus label for family resorts, as does Les Contamines on the same pass.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.0'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','para',1,'Lessons start young. skiresort.com gives the area top marks for families and notes that the ESF runs children''s areas at most base stations, among them Rocharbois, Chamois and Petit Rochebrune in Megève and the Kinderland at Le Bettex. The Pioupiou club at La Caboche, reached by the Chamois gondola from the village, takes children from three in a secure snow garden, with meals included in its five day packages.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','para',2,'Megève starts beginners at Petit Rochebrune, where the Lady tow serves the green Coccinelle, and a beginner pass for the gentle lifts of Rochebrune and Mont d''Arbois costs {{f:F000543}} a day. Above Saint-Gervais a gondola from Le Bettex climbs to Les Marmottons, a beginner area with wide, gradual slopes and the Charlotte la Marmotte play area. For gentle terrain beyond that, Combloux has the highest share of green and blue in the map data, {{f:F000587}}, followed by Princesse and Saint-Gervais at {{f:F000567}}, and Princesse adds a free car park at the foot of its gondola.',array['F000543','F000567','F000587']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','para',3,'Off the slopes, Le Palais in Megève has pools, an ice rink and a climbing wall, and Guide Ski lists a sledge run at Princesse when it is open. On the Jaillet slopes the fun zone of L''Ours des Prés keeps younger children busy.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.paras.3'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','heading',1,'For children','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.listTitle'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','families','note',0,'Sources: <a href="https://guide-ski.fr/?p=8172">Guide Ski for Megève</a>, <a href="https://tourism.saintgervais.com/i-want-to/an-activity/evasion-mont-blanc-ski-resort-saint-gervais-les-bains-en-4359378/">the Saint-Gervais tourist office</a>, <a href="https://www.skiresort.com/en/ski-resort/megeve-saint-gervais/test-result/families-children/">skiresort.com</a>, <a href="https://hautesavoiemontblanc-tourisme.com/en/offers/club-ski-enfants-pioupiou-la-caboche-megeve-en-5830272">Haute-Savoie Mont-Blanc tourism on the Pioupiou club</a> (July 2026), <a href="https://www.haute-savoie-tourisme.org/loisirs/activites-sportives/sports-d-hiver/4965854-les-portes-du-mont-blanc">Haute-Savoie tourism</a> (October 2026) and <a href="https://www.france.fr/fr/article/label-ski-famille-plus/">France.fr on Famille Plus</a> (updated October 2023). Ages and opening times are best checked when booking.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.1.note'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','kicker',0,'Food','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.kicker'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','heading',0,'Eating in Megève and on the mountain','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.h2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','para',0,'Megève holds {{f:F000548|w}} Michelin stars in the 2026 guide. Flocons de Sel, Emmanuel Renaut''s restaurant, has three of them, and La Table de l''Alpaga and Vous one each. Across the network at Saint-Nicolas-de-Véroce, La Table d''Armante won its first star in 2026. Down in the village, Snowcarbon recommends Benjamin for classic bistro cooking and Le Café for seafood, and notes plenty of pizzerias.',array['F000548']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.paras.0'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','para',1,'On the mountain, Snowcarbon picks two very different huts. Le Radaz, a small timber chalet at the head of the Côte 2000 valley, is known for its écorce de sapin, a small Mont d''Or baked in its wooden box. On the Jaillet side the Refuge du Christomet is praised for its rabbit and its steak tartare.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.paras.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','para',2,'Leo Trippi''s guide adds more huts on the Megève side: the Alpage de Pré Rosset, with two terraces facing Mont Blanc, the Auberge Bonjournal on the ridge between Megève and La Giettaz, whose terrace looks all the way round, and La Petite Fontaine at the foot of the red Fontaine run, known for its fondue. Emmanuel Renaut also runs Le Boitet on the Saint-Gervais side, a rustic offshoot of Flocons de Sel with a long wine list.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.paras.2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','para',3,'Above Saint-Gervais, Snowcarbon sends skiers to the Relais des Communailles, a terrace and grill in the forest at the foot of the Communailles lift with Belgian beers on the list, to Sous les Freddy''s below the Bettex-Arbois lift, and to Le Gouet, halfway down towards Saint-Nicolas. In Combloux, Signature occupies a nineteenth century farmhouse facing Mont Blanc.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.paras.3'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','heading',1,'Tables worth the detour','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.listTitle'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','food','note',0,'Michelin 2026: <a href="https://www.alti-mag.com/alti-miam/guide-michelin-2026-la-nouvelle-carte-de-la-gastronomie-alpine">Alti-Mag</a> (March 2026). Restaurants: Snowcarbon for <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/megeve/restaurants-apres-ski-nightlife">Megève</a> and <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/saint-gervais/restaurants-apres-ski-nightlife">Saint-Gervais</a>, and <a href="https://www.leotrippi.com/magazine/resort-guides/best-bars-restaurants-megeve/">Leo Trippi</a> (September 2026). Restaurants change hands and menus each season.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.2.note'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','kicker',0,'Après','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.kicker'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','heading',0,'Après and evenings','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.h2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','para',0,'The loudest afternoon is on the mountain. La Folie Douce opened at the top of Mont Joux, above Saint-Gervais, in {{f:F000507}}, and its terrace looks over the slopes of both resorts with live entertainment every afternoon.',array['F000507']::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.paras.0'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','para',1,'Megève itself is more refined than wild. Snowcarbon describes heated terraces along the pedestrian streets for watching the town go by, and Ski Independence points to the rooftop bar of the Soleil d''Or for a drink with a view.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.paras.1'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','para',2,'Later on, La Ferme Saint-Amour serves dinner and cocktails with live music and DJs, and Les 5 Rues, open since 1952, is a jazz club with live music and cocktails. Cocoon Club and the Rendez-Vous Club stay open late, Leo Trippi adds Le Bar du Lodge, and the Stelsia casino offers another kind of evening.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.paras.2'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','para',3,'Saint-Gervais is quieter but keeps a handful of bars. At the foot of the gondola up to Le Bettex the Oboose Café has live music and DJ sets, Le Nordique mixes cocktails and Les 3 Mousquetons pours local beers and wines. Bar Le Marie Paradis is on the same list, and down at Le Fayet so is the Lovegood Café. The town also has its thermal spa, Les Thermes, in the park at Le Fayet, and Combloux and La Giettaz are quieter still.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.paras.3'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','heading',1,'Where the evenings start','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.listTitle'),
('area:evasion-mont-blanc','apres','note',0,'Sources: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meg%C3%A8ve">Wikipedia on Megève</a> for La Folie Douce, <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/megeve/restaurants-apres-ski-nightlife">Snowcarbon</a>, <a href="https://ski-i.com/france/megeve/apres-ski">Ski Independence</a> (2022), <a href="https://www.leotrippi.com/magazine/resort-guides/best-bars-restaurants-megeve/">Leo Trippi</a> (September 2026), <a href="https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/saint-gervais/restaurants-apres-ski-nightlife">Snowcarbon for Saint-Gervais</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint-Gervais-les-Bains">Wikipedia on Saint-Gervais</a>. Bars open and close from season to season.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','chapters.3.note'),
